      "result": {
        "reply_text": "Your security deposit must be refunded to you on the date of taking over vacant possession of the premises, after making due deduction of any liability of the tenant, as provided under the law.\n\nWhat I understood: Your residential tenancy in Lucknow ended in October 2026, and your landlord has not returned your security deposit of nine crore rupees after you gave back the premises.\n\nWhere you stand: The law states that the security deposit shall be refunded to the tenant on the date of taking over vacant possession of the premises from the tenant, after making due deduction of any liability of the tenant.\n\nYour options in order: You can approach the Rent Authority appointed by the District Collector to file an application accompanied by an affidavit and documents, such as your tenancy agreement.\n\nKeep your tenancy agreement and any proof of handing over vacant possession ready.\n\nWhen to see a lawyer: You may consult a lawyer to help you file your application before the Rent Authority if you need assistance with the procedure.\n\nDo you have the landlord's contact details?\n\nOn what exact date was the tenancy agreement signed?\n\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 11\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 30\nSource: Uttar Pradesh Regulation of Urban Premises Tenancy Act, 2021, section 33\n\nBecause of the points above, please talk to a real lawyer or free legal aid office. (the amount involved is high)\n\nFor free help from a real lawyer or legal aid office:\n- National Legal Services Authority Helpline: 15100 (Source: https://nalsa.gov.in/contact-us/)\n- Uttar Pradesh State Legal Services Authority Contact and Helpline: 1800-419-0234 / 0522-2286395 / 0522-2287972 (Source: http://uttarpradesh.nalsa.gov.in/contact-us/)\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
